        "original_id": "14df23bc-3216-5036-a1d4-8457b5021790",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Trilochanpala, Anandapala\n- Organizations: Kabul Shahis, Shahiya\n- Places: Kabul Valley, Gandhara, eastern Afghanistan, northern Pakistan\n- Topics: Classical Period of India, decline of the Kushan Empire\n\nFacts:\n- The Kabul Shahis, also called Shahiya, ruled the Kabul Valley in eastern Afghanistan and the old province of Gandhara in northern Pakistan from the decline of the Kushan Empire in the 3rd century to the early 11th century during the Classical Period of India.\n- Trilochanpala was the son of Anandapala.\n- Trilochanpala was the last king of the Kabul Shahis.",
